WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.469
-Our guest tonight
is a co-host of "CBS Mornings,

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:06.705
host of the SiriusXM show
"Gayle King in the House,"

00:00:06.705 --> 00:00:10.143
and the editor-at-large
of Oprah Daily.

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.978
The winter issue
of "O Quarterly,"

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:14.147
which features
the 25th anniversary

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:16.582
of Oprah's Favorite Things,
is on stands now.

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:17.984
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:20.119
our friend Gayle King,
everybody!

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:22.221
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:31.431 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:40.673 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:42.575
Welcome back!

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:45.145
-God, there's people!
-I know.

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:47.080
-It's so nice to see people!

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.581
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.450
Oh, my God, Seth.
I don't know about you.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.285
I was just saying
to your team backstage

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:54.120
it's so nice to have people
in the house.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.321
I'm so glad to see you people.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.724
And then you go through
what to wear.

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.225
-Yeah.
Because do you dress up?

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.194
Do you dress down? You know,
my makeup artist said to me,

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:03.229
"Could you please
wear something fun

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.431
instead of what you normally
wear? 'Cause Seth is fun."

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:07.367
So I tried to be
sparkly and fun.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:10.036
-I'm very glad you wore
your Seth clothes.

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:11.804
-These are my Seth clothes.

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:14.440
-And you did me the great
courtesy of being a Zoom guest

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.008
in the time
where we weren't having guests.

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:18.177
So it's so nice to see you again
in person.

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:20.079
-I feel that, too.
-And do you feel like things --

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:21.847
I know you're in a new studio.

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:23.649
-We're in a new studio
in Times Square.

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:25.518
We like that.
-That's great.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.887
-There's a new co-host.
Nate Burleson. Like him.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.489
-He's wonderful.
He's a super-sharp guy.

00:01:30.489 --> 00:01:32.758
-He is. He's very dapper.
He dresses very well.

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:34.793
He's very smart.
We're having a good time.

00:01:34.793 --> 00:01:37.396
But I feel that, you know,
last time I was at home,

00:01:37.396 --> 00:01:38.798
you were at home,
and I kept thinking

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:40.299
there was light
at the end of the tunnel.

00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:41.801
I still feel that.
-Yes.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.703
-I still feel that
because nobody, Seth --

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:45.605
nobody wants to go back
to the way it was.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.173
-No.
-We're not going back

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.274
to the way it was.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:49.709
-We will not go back
to the way it was.

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:51.878
-No.
-And I think one of --

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:54.914
You know, I remember
last year around this time,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.850
it sort of dawned on
I think a lot of us --

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.918
"Oh, maybe I won't travel
for the holidays.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:01.353
Maybe I'm not gonna see my
family for Thanksgiving."

00:02:01.353 --> 00:02:03.489
And it does feel
a little bit more optimistic

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:06.426
in regards to that this year,
and it's really nice to have --

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:08.428
I can't believe this is the
25th year of Favorite Things.

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:09.963
-You know,
this started 25 years ago,

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.131
so just think about Oprah
for a second.

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:16.769
So, it went from the magazine
to the TV show,

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.405
to now we're on digital,
Oprah Daily.

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:21.607
It started 25 years ago
because somebody sent her

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:23.142
a pair of pajamas
that she liked.

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:24.944
-That was it.
-That was it. Karen Neuburger.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:26.379
Because she liked Oprah.
She sent it.

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:29.882
And Oprah believes that life
is always better when shared.

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:32.151
Don't you think?
Always better when shared.

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:33.686
-Yes.
-So she decided that

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:35.988
she would give the pajamas away.

00:02:35.988 --> 00:02:38.057
But anybody who makes
her Favorite Things list,

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:40.326
you had to agree to give it
to the whole studio audience.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.595
It was 300-plus people.
That's how it started.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:43.896
-And people agree--

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:45.732
I mean, I would assume
that's a pretty good trade.

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:47.833
-But you'd be surprised, Seth.
There are a couple of people

00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:49.302
said, "No, we can't do that."
-Really?

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:51.103
-They shall remain nameless.

00:02:51.103 --> 00:02:53.706
-Wow! Forever, by the way.
They're out of business.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:57.043
-I really do want to tell you
because I'm like, "What?!"

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:59.145
-Did you bring anything
for us this time?

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:01.914
-Yes, because, Seth,
I'm so nuts about you.

00:03:01.914 --> 00:03:04.817
-Thank you.
-I love your wife, Alexi.

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:07.820
He's got two adorable boys.
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.055
-Ashe and Axel.
-That's it.

00:03:10.055 --> 00:03:11.191
-Okay, so, the list --

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:12.791
Can I just say something
about the list?

00:03:12.791 --> 00:03:14.694
Over 110 items.

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:16.529
It's the biggest list
we've ever had.

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:19.465
We decided to focus
on women business,

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:22.301
business of people of color,
and small businesses.

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:24.403
-That's businesses
run by babies.

00:03:24.403 --> 00:03:26.205
-Business -- Yeah.
[ Laughs ]

00:03:26.205 --> 00:03:28.107
So, this is --
Oh, I should've let you open it.

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:29.942
This is The Honest Company
from Jessica Alba.

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:31.711
-Oh, my God. Oh, yeah.
We love Jessica Alba.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:34.113
-Don't we love her?
-Yeah. These are great.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:36.048
-Aren't these cute, guys?
-Very cute.

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:38.050
-So we got a set for you...
-Okay.

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:40.286
-...for your lovely wife,
and for your two sons

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.688
and for Frisbee,
there's a matching bandana.

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:44.023
-Really?!
-[ Audience awws ]

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:45.892
-Isn't that good?
I think so, too.

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:48.227
You guys are a good audience.
I like that.

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:50.263
-So, you got my boys
two different colors.

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:51.864
-Yes.
-Which means they're going to

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:55.601
tear the [bleep]
apartment apart.

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:58.538
-But you can [bleep] afford
to fix it.

00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:00.706
-Sold!
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:04.444
-Okay, and...
-Oh, this is -- All right.

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:07.413
-This -- I really like this.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:10.182
-And you better bleep that out.
Otherwise, I won't have a job.

00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:11.417
-I will. I will.
-Okay. So --

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:14.153
-I don't think my wife
is going to wear it.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:17.856
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.856 --> 00:04:22.662
-Seth, do we dare ask audience
what goes on at his house?

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.897
That he pulls out a dog leash...

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.265
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:27.700
-Now we're gonna have to
edit that out.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.435
-I'm going to tell Alexi.
Okay.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:31.504
So, this is from Foggy Dog.
I think this is cool.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:34.173
A bandana, a leash,
and for the doody bags.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:35.308
-Oh, great.

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:36.542
-'Cause I know
you clean up the poop.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:37.810
-Of course. Absolutely.
-I know you do.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.946
-Even when -- when I'm at work,

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:41.547
they call,
and I go all the way back.

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:42.748
This is a bandana for Frisbee?

00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:44.083
-It's for Frisbee.
-Gorgeous.

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:46.151
-So Frisbee we got two things.
-That's really nice.

00:04:46.151 --> 00:04:47.653
-So then I thought this.

00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:51.824
Because the list goes from $13,
which is eye-makeup palette,

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:54.093
all the way over to $2,000,
which is a rower.

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:56.662
I didn't bring the rower,
but I did bring you...

00:04:56.662 --> 00:04:58.197
-Ooh.
-♪ Da-da-da-da ♪

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:00.198
When you're all dressed
in your matching jammies.

00:05:00.198 --> 00:05:01.601
-This is very lovely.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.836
-Eastern Standard waffles.
-Okay.

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.404
-So it comes with --
Isn't that good?

00:05:05.404 --> 00:05:07.573
It comes -- All you have to
do -- Put in the oven.

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:10.008
You got several
different toppings.

00:05:10.008 --> 00:05:12.778
Caramel, my favorite.
Fudge, strawberry.

00:05:12.778 --> 00:05:14.746
-And we --
Actually this is really nice.

00:05:14.746 --> 00:05:17.383
'Cause we're gonna have
a little there, yeah.

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:18.717
So, um --
-Here it is.

00:05:18.717 --> 00:05:20.019
-So, that's caramel sauce.

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:22.455
And that's dark fudge sauce.
Great.

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:24.157
And this won't make a mess
or anything.

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:25.725
And we can just have
a conversation.

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:27.359
-I come bringing gifts
for you, Seth.

00:05:27.359 --> 00:05:29.862
-It's very nice. I am --

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:32.098
-I do.

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:35.734
I got you this pencil.
-Oh. [ Laughs ]

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:37.703
Gosh. For my very own?

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:39.104
-It's your very own!

00:05:39.104 --> 00:05:41.006
But you got something --
you got something --

00:05:41.006 --> 00:05:43.242
A better gift than
I could ever give you this year.

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:45.244
-Ooh, yeah.
-You had a grandson.

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:48.314
-I'm so excited about this.
I have a grandson.

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:50.750
I am somebody's grandmother.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.852
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:55.254
-I mean, I don't know which --
I will start with this.

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:57.022
This is a very --
This is a very cute photo.

00:05:57.022 --> 00:05:59.559
-Yes, yes, yes. This is me
and favorite daughter, Kirby.

00:05:59.559 --> 00:06:02.594 line:0%
Now favorite grandson, Luca.
And this is Slater.

00:06:02.594 --> 00:06:05.831 line:0%
Everybody has to color
coordinate our outfits.

00:06:05.831 --> 00:06:07.066
But there really is something.

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:08.367
You know,
I remember my grandmother.

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:11.370
She seemed a little old.
And I don't feel old at all.

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:13.405
There's something about
seeing your own child

00:06:13.405 --> 00:06:16.875
become a parent that I don't
even know how to explain.

00:06:16.875 --> 00:06:19.779
Listen, I'm not the first person
that has a grandchild. I get it.

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:21.647
But, God, once it happens
to you, it's like --

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:23.315
I want to show you
all the pictures.

00:06:23.315 --> 00:06:25.017
What else you got?
-I'm really happy with this one.

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:28.854
This is his Halloween costume.
Pillsbury Doughboy.

00:06:28.854 --> 00:06:30.923
-What I like about this
is my kids are now the age

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:32.858
where you put them
in their Halloween costume,

00:06:32.858 --> 00:06:34.794
and all it is,
when you take the photo --

00:06:34.794 --> 00:06:36.595
They're at the age where
you're like, "Smile, smile,"

00:06:36.595 --> 00:06:38.497
and trying to get both of them
to smile at the same time

00:06:38.497 --> 00:06:40.632
is an impossibility.
Whereas this is such a fun age

00:06:40.632 --> 00:06:42.668
'cause all you have to worry
about is just propping them.

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:43.902
-No. That's true.

00:06:43.902 --> 00:06:45.537
And that's what we did.
We propped him.

00:06:45.537 --> 00:06:47.272
And then the hand came out,
and you take the picture.

00:06:47.272 --> 00:06:49.174
That's exactly right.

00:06:49.174 --> 00:06:50.843
Lesley Stahl did a book
about grandparents,

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:52.611
and we had her on and I read it,
and I thought,

00:06:52.611 --> 00:06:54.046
"This is a very lovely book,"

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:55.848
but now I want to go back
and read it again.

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:57.316
-Yeah.
-Because I think it'll have

00:06:57.316 --> 00:06:58.851
a totally different meaning.

00:06:58.851 --> 00:07:01.387
May we all feel the love
that we all feel for this child.

00:07:01.387 --> 00:07:02.989
Honest to God.

00:07:02.989 --> 00:07:08.127
-So, my parents sometimes feel
as though we are too strict.

00:07:08.127 --> 00:07:10.696
The parents, you know?
We're too strict to them

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:13.132
insofar as how they treat
the kid and what they do.

00:07:13.132 --> 00:07:15.501
Have you gotten in trouble
with your daughter yet?

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:18.337
-Well, it's funny
you should say that.

00:07:18.337 --> 00:07:19.504
Funny you should say that.

00:07:19.504 --> 00:07:21.240
Because I took a picture
of Luca.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.341
Do you have it?
-I think we have this one.

00:07:23.341 --> 00:07:25.077
It's this one, right? She had
an issue with this photo.

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:27.345
-She had an issue.
-By the way, I want to note...

00:07:27.345 --> 00:07:29.215
I think Luca did, too.

00:07:29.215 --> 00:07:33.419
-But here was the issue.
Because I was "babysitting."

00:07:33.419 --> 00:07:35.220
Listen. Luca is
only seven weeks old.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:36.489
They live in L.A.

00:07:36.489 --> 00:07:38.324
I've been to L.A.
five out of the seven weeks.

00:07:38.324 --> 00:07:41.460
You think they're tired
of seeing me?

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:43.295
"Kirby and Virgil,
can I please come over?"

00:07:43.295 --> 00:07:45.264
Listen, I try to follow
their instructions.

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:46.765
-Yeah.
-So I just thought

00:07:46.765 --> 00:07:49.268
that would be a cute picture,
and she came home and she said,

00:07:49.268 --> 00:07:51.837
"You know,
you didn't put him in properly."

00:07:51.837 --> 00:07:54.874
I said, "Kirby, I just put him
in to take the picture."

00:07:54.874 --> 00:07:56.408
She said,
"Well, we don't do that.

00:07:56.408 --> 00:08:00.246
If you're going to do it, we
like that he's put in properly."

00:08:00.246 --> 00:08:02.048
I said, "But I was
just taking a picture."

00:08:02.048 --> 00:08:03.882
"Doesn't matter.
He has to be put in properly."

00:08:03.882 --> 00:08:06.319
So listen. I'm gonna follow
all the instructions.

00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:08.955
I'm trying not to be that guy,
but it's very --

00:08:08.955 --> 00:08:10.356
You know, I raised two children.

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:12.158
-You don't want
to be the first grandmother

00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:14.226
to have a restraining order.

00:08:14.226 --> 00:08:17.095
-Seth, I raised two children.
I think I did okay.

00:08:17.095 --> 00:08:18.831
But listen.
It is a note to self.

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:20.766
You have to take your lead
from them.

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:22.267
-Yes.
-You do have to take --

00:08:22.267 --> 00:08:24.937
-Hey, what do your kids
call your mom and your dad?

00:08:24.937 --> 00:08:26.872
-Oh, that's
a very good question.

00:08:26.872 --> 00:08:28.908
-'Cause I don't want to
be called Grandma or Nana.

00:08:28.908 --> 00:08:32.511
-We had a jackpot because
my parents talked so long about

00:08:32.511 --> 00:08:35.013
what they wanted to be called,
and it was idiotic.

00:08:35.013 --> 00:08:39.051
Like, my mom was like,
"I think I want to be Mew Mew

00:08:39.051 --> 00:08:41.386
because my grandmother
was Swedish."

00:08:41.386 --> 00:08:43.089
And it's, like, the first
I'm hearing of it.

00:08:43.089 --> 00:08:45.924
I'm like, "You're not going to
be Mew Mew. What are you talk--"

00:08:45.924 --> 00:08:47.326
-I've met your mom.
She's lovely.

00:08:47.326 --> 00:08:50.329
-She is lovely. But they
were approaching this wrong.

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:53.665
Then my oldest, the first time
he said, "Grandpa,"

00:08:53.665 --> 00:08:55.867
he pronounced it "Ponka,"

00:08:55.867 --> 00:08:59.404
And so we call --
My parents are the Ponkas.

00:08:59.404 --> 00:09:01.506
-See? I like that. I like that.

00:09:01.506 --> 00:09:02.841
-And they're Larry and Hillary,

00:09:02.841 --> 00:09:05.277
and so they're Ponka-arry
and Ponka-hury.

00:09:05.277 --> 00:09:07.179
And it's perfect.
And they're growing.

00:09:07.179 --> 00:09:09.048
It's absolutely --
It's organic and natural.

00:09:09.048 --> 00:09:10.315
And so I like that you're trying

00:09:10.315 --> 00:09:12.084
to decide what
you're going to be called,

00:09:12.084 --> 00:09:13.686
but I think
you've got to let them --

00:09:13.686 --> 00:09:15.988
-Yeah, people keep saying
they'll make up their own name.

00:09:15.988 --> 00:09:18.257
But I have had some suggestions,
Seth.

00:09:18.257 --> 00:09:20.593
-Do you get suggestions
from you-know-who?

00:09:20.593 --> 00:09:24.196
-Well, the suggestion
I have for myself is Gaia,

00:09:24.196 --> 00:09:26.065
which, by the way, guys,
means "Mother Earth."

00:09:26.065 --> 00:09:28.366
And it kind of sounds
like "Gayle."

00:09:28.366 --> 00:09:31.370
But I don't want to be called
Gail by my grandchild.

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:34.106
So I came up with Gaia,
which I thought was very nice.

00:09:34.106 --> 00:09:37.009
Oprah. You all know her.

00:09:37.009 --> 00:09:39.578
-Yeah.
-She suggested Oprah.

00:09:39.578 --> 00:09:40.780
-She --

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:43.849
[ Laughter ]

00:09:43.849 --> 00:09:46.685
That's good.
Well, she's very opinionated.

00:09:46.685 --> 00:09:48.821
She said, "Gaia.
That sounds pretentious."

00:09:48.821 --> 00:09:50.889
Do you guys think
it sounds pretentious?

00:09:50.889 --> 00:09:52.824
-Kinda?
-It's a little --

00:09:52.824 --> 00:09:55.127
It's a little pretentious.
-Do you think so?

00:09:55.127 --> 00:09:58.230
See? Oh, Seth.
God, you're hurting me.

00:09:58.230 --> 00:10:00.299
And then Kirby said,
favorite daughter Kirby said,

00:10:00.299 --> 00:10:03.569
"Mom, that's very extra."
So, I had said Gaia.

00:10:03.569 --> 00:10:05.838
I was walking down the street
on 8th Avenue,

00:10:05.838 --> 00:10:08.341
and a woman walked up to me,
and she said,

00:10:08.341 --> 00:10:10.242
"I don't know
what's wrong with you.

00:10:10.242 --> 00:10:11.810
I hear you want
to be called..."

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:14.947
She said, "Gai-anne or whatever
you want to call yourself."

00:10:14.947 --> 00:10:16.582
What's wrong with Grandma?"

00:10:16.582 --> 00:10:18.416
And then she just turned around
and walked off.

00:10:18.416 --> 00:10:19.718
But the way she said,

00:10:19.718 --> 00:10:21.620
"Gai-anne or whatever
you want to call yourself.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.789
That don't even make no sense.
What's wrong with Grandma?"

00:10:23.789 --> 00:10:24.990
And then she just walked off.

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:26.658
"Thank you, ma'am.
It's so nice to meet you."

00:10:26.658 --> 00:10:29.328
Wait a second, Seth. I'm being
very serious about that.

00:10:29.328 --> 00:10:30.695
You think it sounds pretentious?

00:10:30.695 --> 00:10:33.866
-I think "Gaia" --
I think the fact that "Gaia"

00:10:33.866 --> 00:10:38.003
means "Mother Earth"
is the problem with it.

00:10:38.003 --> 00:10:39.338
-But, Seth, that's what --

00:10:39.338 --> 00:10:42.274
-I would go with, like, GoGo.
Like, just have --

00:10:42.274 --> 00:10:45.043
Like, it shouldn't
have a meaning.

00:10:45.043 --> 00:10:47.379
-But, Seth, I thought that
that was endearing.

00:10:47.379 --> 00:10:48.714
-Mm-hmm.

00:10:48.714 --> 00:10:50.649
[ Laughter ]

00:10:50.649 --> 00:10:54.753
-Guys, don't encourage him!
Don't encourage him.

00:10:54.753 --> 00:10:56.955
-If you leave
with anything today,

00:10:56.955 --> 00:11:00.392
it's this --
you can't win 'em all.

00:11:00.392 --> 00:11:02.728
-Okay. No. Maybe I'll be --
What is it? Ponka?

00:11:02.728 --> 00:11:04.096
-Ponka. Ponka.

00:11:04.096 --> 00:11:06.098
We want Ponka to take off.
Ponka Gayle.

00:11:06.098 --> 00:11:07.999
-Okay. Ponka. All right.
-All right.

00:11:07.999 --> 00:11:10.369
I have a -- I want to give you
one last opportunity.

00:11:10.369 --> 00:11:11.737
I want to make up for the fact

00:11:11.737 --> 00:11:13.272
that I have not supported you
on Gaia.

00:11:13.272 --> 00:11:14.606
-Yes.

00:11:14.606 --> 00:11:16.808
-Taylor Swift is coming here
tomorrow.

00:11:16.808 --> 00:11:18.977
-Tomorrow. Do you know
how much I like Taylor Swift?

00:11:18.977 --> 00:11:20.145
-I do know how much you like.

00:11:20.145 --> 00:11:21.447
-I've been to four
of Taylor's concerts.

00:11:21.447 --> 00:11:22.647
I really like her.

00:11:22.647 --> 00:11:24.149
When she was sending out
those cardigan sweaters,

00:11:24.149 --> 00:11:25.718
did you get one? I did.

00:11:25.718 --> 00:11:26.919
-I did not.

00:11:26.919 --> 00:11:28.120
-I did.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:31.289
-Point, Gaia.

00:11:31.289 --> 00:11:32.958
-Oh, but I like her
so much love.

00:11:32.958 --> 00:11:35.728
-She's lovely. But I want to
give you the opportunity.

00:11:35.728 --> 00:11:37.763
-She's here tomorrow.
And I'm here today.

00:11:37.763 --> 00:11:39.465
-You're here today.
-Thanks, Seth.

00:11:39.465 --> 00:11:42.534
-You're welcome.
-Thanks, Mike. Thanks. Thanks.

00:11:42.534 --> 00:11:44.336
But I'm really glad to see you.

00:11:44.336 --> 00:11:46.071
-But you want to -- I wanted
to give you the opportunity

00:11:46.071 --> 00:11:47.539
to leave something for Taylor.

00:11:47.539 --> 00:11:49.141
-Okay.
This is what I was thinking.

00:11:49.141 --> 00:11:50.809
Because you like
the pajamas so much.

00:11:50.809 --> 00:11:52.144
I actually have
a matching pair, too.

00:11:52.144 --> 00:11:53.679
-Okay. I think
it's on the other side of you.

00:11:53.679 --> 00:11:54.880
-Where is it?
-On the other side.

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:56.815
Right over there.
-Okay. Good.

00:11:56.815 --> 00:11:58.951
So, I thought when she comes --

00:11:58.951 --> 00:12:01.386
And, Seth, I would like
an on-camera presentation.

00:12:01.386 --> 00:12:02.688
-Okay. Gotcha.

00:12:02.688 --> 00:12:03.955
-You guys know
that's not happening.

00:12:03.955 --> 00:12:05.724
I would like
an on-camera presentation

00:12:05.724 --> 00:12:08.394
to say Gayle was here yesterday
and she brought this for you.

00:12:08.394 --> 00:12:10.429
And so I thought
it would be nice for her

00:12:10.429 --> 00:12:12.998
to have a pair of pajamas
like you have and I have.

00:12:12.998 --> 00:12:15.200
Then we could all come over
to your place.

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:16.469
-Okay.
-Me and Taylor.

00:12:16.469 --> 00:12:18.003
-I mean, it sounds good.
-For breakfast.

00:12:18.003 --> 00:12:21.674
-I'm just -- I don't want you
to ever say that I lied to you.

00:12:21.674 --> 00:12:23.208
So I'm going to tell you now

00:12:23.208 --> 00:12:26.278
I will tell her
it's from both of us.

00:12:26.278 --> 00:12:28.781
-Okay. Fair enough.

00:12:28.781 --> 00:12:32.617
-Gaia King, everybody!
Mother Earth!

00:12:32.617 --> 00:12:34.519
The winter issue of
"O Quarterly" is on stands now.

00:12:34.519 --> 00:12:36.288
And Oprah's Favorite Things
are also available

00:12:36.288 --> 00:12:38.424
at OprahDaily.com and Amazon.

